/* sys.yon — the package file of `sys`, under prelude/.
 *
 * The face of the operating system. SystemOs is the one place whose
 * primitives reach the kernel: memory, shared memory, the wait on a word,
 * the clocks, the arguments, writing, processes. A Region is memory the
 * kernel gave: an opaque handle, owned by whoever asked for it. The rest of
 * the prelude is Yon written on top of this. */
topos where {
}
